cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository in academic work, please cite it, and also cite PyBoy and the DeepSeek API you rely on."
title: "Pokemon Red Autonomous Agent - Vision-Based Autonomous Exploration and Multi-Agent Decision-Making"
abstract: >-
  A research codebase for studying vision-based autonomous agents on a real
  Game Boy game. A vision large language model (DeepSeek) observes only the
  emulator screen, its own action history and its own notes, and controls the
  game through constrained button presses. The repository implements pure-vision
  localization and permanent grid/world maps (Navigation v2), a Game Director
  with single-owner control arbitration, and independent Story and Pokemon
  agents for dialogue and battle takeover, together with task scheduling,
  shared memory, progress monitoring, checkpoint rollback and API budgeting.
  No game ROM, save state, model weights, gameplay video or API key is
  distributed. The previous PPO training reproduction is archived on the
  `archive/ppo-reproduction` branch.
